* Bounded early-cooling diagnostic; no production input overwritten.
* Production candidate: v6 conditions confirmed by user 2026-11-01.
* v6 copy of v5: 24.4 MeV, 200 microA; previous inputs preserved.
* 1 mm target: 0.200 g Ra226 as RaCl2 plus 0.5100 g graphite.
* Density derived from fixed masses and pi*(1 cm)^2*(0.1 cm).
* Recommended executable: /usr/local/fluka/bin/flukadpm; no run performed.
* Working copy: configure here with the native FLUKA preprocessor.
* Original cyclotron_activation.inp is preserved. No generator required.
* Negative BEAM energy is GeV; baseline 24.4 MeV at source.
#define EBEAM 0.0244
* Graphite partial density (g carbon/cm3 mixture); fixed Ra/Cl loading.
#define CRHO 1.6233804195373
#define RARHO 0.63661977236758
#define CLRHO 0.19971832681797
#define RHOM 2.4597185187229
* Keep RHOM = CRHO + RARHO + CLRHO; case generator updates both.
* Proton scoring range: raise EMAX above highest requested source energy.
#define EMAX 0.0245
#define NEBIN 1200
* Seven days in seconds; 200 microA singly charged protons in particles/s.
#define IRRT 604800
#define RATE 1248301814892200
#define NHIST 200000
#define SEED 54238137
* Energy cutoffs in GeV; electron value below is kinetic energy.
#define ECUT 0.0001
#define GCUT 1E-06
#define NTEMP 296
* Neutron library is set literally on LOW-PWXS: JEFF-3.3.
* Keep this hyphenated name out of #define expression evaluation.
* Defined switches are ON. Remove or #undef to turn OFF; value 0 is ON.
#define PHNUC
#define PENETR
* Cartesian fluence maps: cm, bin counts; shared grid for all particles.
#define XYZMAP
#define XYMAX 1.3
#define ZMIN -0.02
#define ZMAX 1.8
#define NXY 51
#define NZ 260
TITLE
Target2 v6: 24.4 MeV, 200 microA, 1 mm target, 0.5100 g graphite
DEFAULTS                                                              PRECISIO
* Current beam retained: Gaussian x/y FWHM 1.6 cm; no divergence.
BEAM         -$EBEAM       0.0       0.0      -1.6      -1.6       1.0PROTON
BEAMPOS          0.0       0.0      -5.0
* Supplied MCNP x axis mapped to FLUKA +z; target front z=0.155 cm.
GEOBEGIN                                                              COMBNAME
    0    0          Enclosed target: one Al housing, one exterior vacuum
SPH world      0 0 0.255 10
SPH det100     0 0 0.205 100
SPH far        0 0 0.205 110
XYP dp01       98.6857753012
XYP dp02       94.1742620786
XYP dp03       86.8075403784
XYP dp04       76.8094443119
XYP dp05       64.4837609687
XYP dp06       50.205
XYP dp07       34.4070143326
XYP dp08       17.5698177667
XYP dp09       0.205
XYP dp10       -17.1598177667
XYP dp11       -33.9970143326
XYP dp12       -49.795
XYP dp13       -64.0737609687
XYP dp14       -76.3994443119
XYP dp15       -86.3975403784
XYP dp16       -93.7642620786
XYP dp17       -98.2757753012
* Housing outer envelope; inner cavity starts behind 0.5 mm Al front.
RCC outer      0 0 0 0 0 1.655 1.2
RCC inner      0 0 0.05 0 0 1.405 1
* Only four internal interfaces; cavity RCC defines its two ends.
XYP watend     0.15
XYP taend      0.155
XYP tgtend     0.255
XYP cuend      0.455
END
BLKHOLE      5 -far
VACREG       5 +world -outer
ALCASE       5 +outer -inner
WAT          5 +inner +watend
TAWIN        5 +inner -watend +taend
CUBACK       5 +inner -tgtend +cuend
COOL         5 +inner -cuend
TGT          5 +inner -taend +tgtend
DET01        5 +det100 -world -dp01
DET02        5 +det100 -world +dp01 -dp02
DET03        5 +det100 -world +dp02 -dp03
DET04        5 +det100 -world +dp03 -dp04
DET05        5 +det100 -world +dp04 -dp05
DET06        5 +det100 -world +dp05 -dp06
DET07        5 +det100 -world +dp06 -dp07
DET08        5 +det100 -world +dp07 -dp08
DET09        5 +det100 -world +dp08 -dp09
DET10        5 +det100 -world +dp09 -dp10
DET11        5 +det100 -world +dp10 -dp11
DET12        5 +det100 -world +dp11 -dp12
DET13        5 +det100 -world +dp12 -dp13
DET14        5 +det100 -world +dp13 -dp14
DET15        5 +det100 -world +dp14 -dp15
DET16        5 +det100 -world +dp15 -dp16
DET17        5 +det100 -world +dp16 -dp17
DET18        5 +det100 -world +dp17
OUTDET       5 +far -det100
END
GEOEND
* Elemental materials for Al6061 alloy.
MATERIAL          24                7.19                              CHROMIUM
MATERIAL          25                7.21                              MANGANES
* Al 6061: supplied MCNP M1 mass proportions, density 2.7 g/cm3.
MATERIAL          30               7.133                              ZINC
MATERIAL                             2.7                              AL6061
COMPOUND       -0.01  MAGNESIU    -0.972  ALUMINUM    -0.006   SILICONAL6061
COMPOUND   -0.000876  TITANIUM  -0.00195  CHROMIUM -0.000876  MANGANESAL6061
COMPOUND   -0.004088      IRON  -0.00275    COPPER  -0.00146      ZINCAL6061
* v3: exact 0.200 g Ra226; Cl from RaCl2 stoichiometry (226,35.45).
* Graphite mass 0.5100 g; homogeneous anhydrous mixture.
MATERIAL          88                 5.5                           226RADIUM
MATERIAL          17           0.0029947                              CHLORINE
MATERIAL          73              16.654                           181TANTALUM
MATERIAL          29                8.96                            63CU63
MATERIAL          29                8.96                            65CU65
MATERIAL                            8.96                              CUMIX
COMPOUND      0.6917      CU63    0.3083      CU65                    CUMIX
MATERIAL                           $RHOM                              RACL2
COMPOUND     -$RARHO    RADIUM    -$CRHO    CARBON   -$CLRHO  CHLORINERACL2
